ERIS Alembic Migrations
=======================

Run all alembic commands from the backend/ directory, where alembic.ini
and backend/.env are located.

Quick reference
---------------
  alembic current               Show current revision on the connected DB
  alembic history --verbose     Show full migration history
  alembic heads                 Show revision(s) with no children (= "head")
  alembic upgrade head          Apply all pending migrations
  alembic upgrade +1            Apply the next migration only
  alembic upgrade --sql head    Preview SQL without executing it
  alembic stamp 0001_baseline   Mark an existing DB at baseline (one-time)
  alembic revision -m "..."     Create a new migration file

Helper scripts (run from backend/)
-----------------------------------
  .\migrate.ps1 <command>       Windows PowerShell
  ./migrate.sh <command>        Linux / Proxmox server

Never run
---------
  Do NOT put real credentials in alembic.ini.
  DB credentials are read from backend/.env via app settings.

Full procedures, backup commands, and Proxmox deployment instructions:
  docs/MIGRATIONS.md
